{"code":"de","name":"German","native":"Deutsch","phase":1,"medium":"en","file_level":"B1","level":{"title":"Intermediate: stories, opinions, work, plans","goals":["Tell stories with Perfekt and Präteritum","Compare things and argue opinions politely","Handle work talk and make future plans"],"units":[{"id":"B1-U1","title":"Stories and opinions","lessons":[{"id":"B1-U1-L1","title":"Stories: Perfekt vs Präteritum","learn":"Two pasts! PERFEKT = spoken past (ICH HABE GESEHEN = I saw). PRÄTERITUM = story past for a few verbs: WAR (was), HATTE (had), DACHTE (thought). Stories mix: ES WAR SONNIG, ICH HABE GEFEIERT.","vocab":[{"t":"gestern","r":"GES-tern","en":"yesterday","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"die Woche","r":"dee VOH-khuh","en":"week","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Jahr","r":"dahss yahr","en":"year","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Mal","r":"dahss mahl","en":"time (occasion)","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Geschichte","r":"dee guh-SHEEKH-tuh","en":"story","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Party","r":"dee PAHR-tee","en":"party","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Geschenk","r":"dahss guh-SHENK","en":"gift","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Überraschung","r":"dee ew-ber-RAH-shoong","en":"surprise","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Perfekt vs Präteritum: gesehen vs war","explain":"ICH HABE GESEHEN = I saw (spoken). ICH WAR = I was (story). ICH HATTE = I had. Rule: war/hatte/dachte/wollte live in Präteritum; almost everything else uses Perfekt in speech.","pattern":"Perfekt (habe + GE-) · Präteritum (war/hatte/dachte)","examples":[{"t":"Ich bin um acht Uhr angekommen.","r":"eekh been oom ahkht oor AHN-guh-koh-men.","en":"I arrived at eight. (Perfekt)"},{"t":"Es war sonnig.","r":"ess vahr ZON-nikh.","en":"It was sunny. (Präteritum)"},{"t":"Ich dachte, du kommst mit.","r":"eekh DAHKH-tuh, doo kohmst mit.","en":"I thought you come along."}],"mistakes":["Saying ES HAT SONNIG GEWESEN — weather is simply ES WAR.","Saying ICH HABE GEDACHT in stories — storytellers say ICH DACHTE."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Lena","t":"Gestern war ich auf einer Party.","r":"GES-tern vahr eekh owf EY-ner PAHR-tee.","en":"Yesterday I was at a party."},{"sp":"Max","t":"Wie war sie?","r":"vee vahr zee?","en":"How was it?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Sie war toll. Es gab Musik und wir haben getanzt.","r":"zee vahr tohl. ess gahp moo-ZEEK oont veer HAH-ben guh-TAHNTST.","en":"It was great. There was music and we danced."},{"sp":"Max","t":"Klasse!","r":"KLAH-suh!","en":"Awesome!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: It was sunny","answer":"Es war sonnig"},{"type":"fill","q":"Ich bin um acht Uhr ___ (arrived)","answer":"angekommen"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I thought' (story) is…","options":["ich habe gedacht","ich dachte","ich denke","ich werde denken"],"answer":"ich dachte"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: war / ich / Party / einer / auf","answer":"ich war auf einer Party"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Gestern war ich auf einer Party.","answer":"Gestern war ich auf einer Party."}],"quiz":[{"q":"PERFEKT vs PRÄTERITUM: the difference is…","options":["I/you","spoken vs story past","loud/quiet","past/future"],"answer":1,"why":"Perfekt speaks; Präteritum narrates key verbs."},{"q":"ES WAR SONNIG means…","options":["it is sunny","it was sunny","it will rain","it snowed"],"answer":1,"why":"War = was."},{"q":"DAS GESCHENK is…","options":["party","gift","story","surprise"],"answer":1,"why":"Geschenk = gift."},{"q":"WIE WAR SIE? means…","options":["How was it?","Where was it?","When was it?","Who was it?"],"answer":0,"why":"Wie + war = how was."},{"q":"Which lives in Präteritum?","options":["gesehen","gegessen","war","getrunken"],"answer":2,"why":"War (was) is the story form."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Past stories worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["yesterday","party","gift"],"key":["gestern","die Party","das Geschenk"]},{"instruction":"Choose Perfekt or Präteritum.","items":["I arrived (spoken)","It was sunny (story)","I thought (story)"],"key":["ich bin angekommen","es war sonnig","ich dachte"]},{"instruction":"Start a story (two lines).","items":["Yesterday I was at …","It was …"],"key":["Gestern war ich …","Es/Sie war …"]}]}},{"id":"B1-U1-L2","title":"Opinions and comparisons","learn":"Compare with Komparativ + ALS (than): GRÖßER ALS = bigger than. Superlativ: AM GRÖßTEN = the biggest. Specials: BESSER (better), AM BESTEN (best). Opinions: ICH FINDE (I find), MEINER MEINUNG NACH (in my opinion).","vocab":[{"t":"besser","r":"BES-ser","en":"better","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"schlechter","r":"SHLEKH-ter","en":"worse","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"gleich","r":"gleyekh","en":"same","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"anders","r":"AHN-ders","en":"different","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"die Meinung","r":"dee MEY-noong","en":"opinion","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Grund","r":"dehr groont","en":"reason","pos":"noun"},{"t":"mehr","r":"mehr","en":"more","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"weniger","r":"VEH-nee-ger","en":"less","pos":"adverb"}],"grammar":{"title":"Komparativ + als, Superlativ am …-sten","explain":"GRÖßER ALS = bigger than. AM GRÖßTEN = the biggest. Umlaut jumps in: GROSS → GRÖßER. BESSER and SCHLECHTER never take MEHR — complete already!","pattern":"-er + als · am + -sten","examples":[{"t":"Es ist größer als mein Haus.","r":"ess ist GRUR-ser ahls meyen hows.","en":"It is bigger than my house."},{"t":"Dieses Buch ist besser.","r":"DEE-zess bookh ist BES-ser.","en":"This book is better."},{"t":"Ich finde, es ist schlechter.","r":"eekh FIN-duh, ess ist SHLEKH-ter.","en":"I find it worse."}],"mistakes":["Saying MEHR BESSER — just BESSER!","Saying GRÖßER WIE — than is ALS, not wie!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Max","t":"Ich finde, dieses Café ist besser.","r":"eekh FIN-duh, DEE-zess kah-FEH ist BES-ser.","en":"I find this café better."},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Meiner Meinung nach ist das andere billiger.","r":"MEY-ner MEY-noong nahkh ist dahss AHN-duh-ruh BIL-lee-ger.","en":"In my opinion the other one is cheaper."},{"sp":"Max","t":"Du hast recht, aber dieses ist schöner.","r":"doo hahst rekht, AH-ber DEE-zess ist SHUR-ner.","en":"You are right, but this one is prettier."},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Einverstanden!","r":"EYEN-fehr-shtahn-den!","en":"Agreed!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: This book is better","answer":"Dieses Buch ist besser"},{"type":"fill","q":"Es ist größer ___ mein Haus. (than)","answer":"als"},{"type":"choose","q":"'In my opinion' is…","options":["Ich finde","Meiner Meinung nach","Du hast recht","Klasse"],"answer":"Meiner Meinung nach"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: recht / hast / du","answer":"du hast recht"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ich finde, es ist besser.","answer":"Ich finde, es ist besser."}],"quiz":[{"q":"GRÖßER ALS means…","options":["big and good","bigger than","very big","big house"],"answer":1,"why":"-Er + als = more…than."},{"q":"Why no MEHR with BESSER?","options":["it is ugly","besser already means better","it is slang","it is formal"],"answer":1,"why":"Besser = better, complete."},{"q":"DU HAST RECHT means…","options":["you are wrong","you are right","you are late","you are lost"],"answer":1,"why":"Recht haben = to be right."},{"q":"DAS ANDERE is…","options":["the same","the other one","the best","the shop"],"answer":1,"why":"Andere = other."},{"q":"ICH FINDE means…","options":["I know","I find/think","I see","I want"],"answer":1,"why":"Ich finde = I find."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Opinions worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["better","different","opinion"],"key":["besser","anders","die Meinung"]},{"instruction":"Compare (use als).","items":["My house / big / yours","This café / cheap / that one"],"key":["Mein Haus ist größer als deins","Dieses Café ist billiger als das dort"]},{"instruction":"Give your opinion.","items":["I find this book better","You are right"],"key":["Ich finde, dieses Buch ist besser","Du hast recht"]}]}}]},{"id":"B1-U2","title":"Real world","lessons":[{"id":"B1-U2-L1","title":"Work and SIE (formal you)","learn":"At work, use SIE (capital S!) with strangers and bosses. SIE takes -EN verbs: SIE SPRECHEN. DU is for friends; SIE is respect. Small sie = she/they; BIG SIE = formal you!","vocab":[{"t":"die Arbeit","r":"dee AHR-beyet","en":"work / job","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Büro","r":"dahss bew-ROH","en":"office","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Chef","r":"dehr shef","en":"boss","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Besprechung","r":"dee buh-SHPREH-khoong","en":"meeting","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die E-Mail","r":"dee EE-mayl","en":"email","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Projekt","r":"dahss proh-YEKT","en":"project","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Kunde","r":"dehr KOON-duh","en":"client","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Zeitplan","r":"dehr TSEYET-plahn","en":"schedule","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"SIE: formal you takes -EN","explain":"DU SPRICHST (friend) vs SIE SPRECHEN (formal). SIE SIND (you are), SIE HABEN (you have). Capital S or it's she/they — the capital letter IS the respect!","pattern":"SIE + -en verb (sprechen, sind, haben)","examples":[{"t":"Sprechen Sie Englisch?","r":"SHPREH-khen zee ENG-lish?","en":"Do you (formal) speak English?"},{"t":"Wie geht es Ihnen?","r":"vee gayt ess EE-nen?","en":"How are you? (formal)"},{"t":"Sie haben recht.","r":"zee HAH-ben rekht.","en":"You (formal) are right."}],"mistakes":["Using DU with a new boss — start with SIE.","Writing small sie for formal — formal SIE is CAPITAL."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Max","t":"Guten Tag. Wie geht es Ihnen?","r":"GOO-ten tahk. vee gayt ess EE-nen?","en":"Hello. How are you? (formal)"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Danke, gut. Und Ihnen?","r":"DAHN-kuh, goot. oont EE-nen?","en":"Thanks, fine. And you?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Gut. Wann ist die Besprechung?","r":"goot. vahn ist dee buh-SHPREH-khoong?","en":"Fine. When is the meeting?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Um zehn Uhr, im Büro.","r":"oom tsehn oor, im bew-ROH.","en":"At ten, in the office."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say (formal): Do you speak English?","answer":"Sprechen Sie Englisch?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Wie geht es ___? (formal you)","answer":"Ihnen"},{"type":"choose","q":"To a new boss you use…","options":["du","Sie","ihr","er"],"answer":"Sie"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: Ihnen / geht / es / wie","answer":"wie geht es Ihnen"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Wie geht es Ihnen?","answer":"Wie geht es Ihnen?"}],"quiz":[{"q":"SIE takes which ending?","options":["-e","-st","-en","-t"],"answer":2,"why":"Sie + sprechen/sind/haben."},{"q":"DER CHEF is…","options":["office","boss","client","mail"],"answer":1,"why":"Chef = boss."},{"q":"SPRECHEN SIE ENGLISCH? (formal) means…","options":["He speaks English","Do you speak English?","She likes English","Speak English!"],"answer":1,"why":"Formal you, -EN form."},{"q":"DIE BESPRECHUNG is…","options":["office","project","meeting","schedule"],"answer":2,"why":"Besprechung = meeting."},{"q":"Formal SIE is written…","options":["small","CAPITAL","it varies","never"],"answer":1,"why":"Capital S = respect."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Work worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["office","boss","meeting"],"key":["das Büro","der Chef","die Besprechung"]},{"instruction":"Make it formal (Sie).","items":["Do you speak English?","How are you?","You are right."],"key":["Sprechen Sie Englisch?","Wie geht es Ihnen?","Sie haben recht"]},{"instruction":"Ask about the meeting.","items":["When is the meeting?","At ten, in the office"],"key":["Wann ist die Besprechung?","Um zehn Uhr, im Büro"]}]}},{"id":"B1-U2-L2","title":"Wishes: ich möchte","learn":"Dream big! ICH MÖCHTE (I would like) + verb-at-end: ICH MÖCHTE REISEN = I would like to travel. ICH HOFFE (I hope) opens plans: ICH HOFFE ZU REISEN = I hope to travel.","vocab":[{"t":"die Zukunft","r":"dee TSOO-koonft","en":"future","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Traum","r":"dehr trowm","en":"dream","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Wunsch","r":"dehr voonsh","en":"wish","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Plan","r":"dehr plahn","en":"plan","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Reise","r":"dee RY-zuh","en":"trip","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Glück","r":"dahss glewk","en":"luck","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Hoffnung","r":"dee HOHF-noong","en":"hope","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Schicksal","r":"dahss SHIK-zahl","en":"destiny","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Soft wishes: ich möchte + verb (end)","explain":"ICH MÖCHTE = I would like. The main verb jumps to the END: ICH MÖCHTE DEUTSCH LERNEN (I would like to learn German). Bookends again: möchte … lernen!","pattern":"ich möchte + … + verb (end)","examples":[{"t":"Ich möchte reisen.","r":"eekh MURKH-tuh REY-zen.","en":"I would like to travel."},{"t":"Ich hoffe zu reisen.","r":"eekh HOH-fuh tsoo REY-zen.","en":"I hope to travel."},{"t":"Viel Glück!","r":"feel glewk!","en":"Good luck!"}],"mistakes":["Putting the verb early: ICH MÖCHTE REISEN (end!) — never ICH REISE MÖCHTE.","Saying ICH WILL for soft wishes — MÖCHTE is kinder."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Lena","t":"Was sind deine Pläne?","r":"vahss zint DEY-nuh PLEH-nuh?","en":"What are your plans?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Ich möchte nach Spanien reisen.","r":"eekh MURKH-tuh nahkh SHPAN-yen REY-zen.","en":"I would like to travel to Spain."},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Ich hoffe! Fahren wir zusammen?","r":"eekh HOH-fuh! FAH-ren veer tsoo-ZAH-men?","en":"I hope so! Shall we go together?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Viel Glück!","r":"feel glewk!","en":"Good luck!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I would like to travel","answer":"Ich möchte reisen"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ Glück! (Much)","answer":"Viel"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I hope to travel' is…","options":["Ich hoffe zu reisen","Ich möchte reisen","Ich will reisen","Ich habe gereist"],"answer":"Ich hoffe zu reisen"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: reisen / möchte / nach / Spanien / ich","answer":"ich möchte nach Spanien reisen"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ich möchte nach Spanien reisen.","answer":"Ich möchte nach Spanien reisen."}],"quiz":[{"q":"ICH MÖCHTE REISEN means…","options":["I travel now","I would like to travel","I travelled","I must travel"],"answer":1,"why":"Möchte + verb = soft wish."},{"q":"ICH HOFFE means…","options":["maybe","I hope","goodbye","never"],"answer":1,"why":"Hoffe = hope."},{"q":"DER TRAUM is…","options":["plan","dream","luck","trip"],"answer":1,"why":"Traum = dream."},{"q":"After MÖCHTE the verb goes…","options":["second","to the end","first","nowhere"],"answer":1,"why":"Ich möchte … REISEN."},{"q":"VIEL GLÜCK! means…","options":["Have fun!","Good luck!","Well done!","See you!"],"answer":1,"why":"Viel Glück = good luck."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Wishes worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["dream","luck","hope"],"key":["der Traum","das Glück","die Hoffnung"]},{"instruction":"Make soft wishes.","items":["I would like to learn","I would like to travel"],"key":["Ich möchte lernen","Ich möchte reisen"]},{"instruction":"Talk about plans.","items":["What are your plans?","Good luck!"],"key":["Was sind deine Pläne?","Viel Glück!"]}]}}]},{"id":"B1-U3","title":"Plans and media","lessons":[{"id":"B1-U3-L1","title":"Future plans (werden)","learn":"Full future with WERDEN: ICH WERDE REISEN (I will travel), DU WIRST, ER WIRD. Time words join in: BALD (soon), NÄCHSTES JAHR (next year). Main verb still jumps to the end!","vocab":[{"t":"reisen","r":"REY-zen","en":"to travel","pos":"verb"},{"t":"studieren","r":"shtoo-DEE-ren","en":"to study","pos":"verb"},{"t":"arbeiten","r":"AHR-beyeten","en":"to work","pos":"verb"},{"t":"lernen","r":"LEHR-nen","en":"to learn","pos":"verb"},{"t":"sparen","r":"SHPAR-ren","en":"to save (money)","pos":"verb"},{"t":"umziehen","r":"OOM-tsee-en","en":"to move house","pos":"verb"},{"t":"bald","r":"bahlt","en":"soon","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"nächstes Jahr","r":"NEHKH-stess yahr","en":"next year","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Future: ich werde … verb (end)","explain":"ICH WERDE REISEN, DU WIRST LERNEN, ER WIRD ARBEITEN. WERDEN carries will; the main verb waits at the end. Germans also use present + time word: ICH REISE MORGEN (I travel tomorrow)!","pattern":"ich werde/du wirst/er wird + … + verb","examples":[{"t":"Ich werde bald reisen.","r":"eekh VEHR-duh bahlt REY-zen.","en":"I will travel soon."},{"t":"Wirst du Deutsch lernen?","r":"veerst doo doytch LEHR-nen?","en":"Will you learn German?"},{"t":"Er wird schnell lernen.","r":"ehr veert shnel LEHR-nen.","en":"He will learn fast."}],"mistakes":["Putting the verb second: ICH WERDE BALD REISEN (REISEN last!).","Saying DU WERDE — you is DU WIRST."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Max","t":"Was wirst du nächstes Jahr machen?","r":"vahss veerst doo NEHKH-stess yahr MAH-khen?","en":"What will you do next year?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Ich werde nach Spanien reisen und Deutsch lernen.","r":"eekh VEHR-duh nahkh SHPAN-yen REY-zen oont doytch LEHR-nen.","en":"I will travel to Spain and learn German."},{"sp":"Max","t":"Du wirst schnell lernen!","r":"doo veerst shnel LEHR-nen!","en":"You will learn fast!"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Ich hoffe!","r":"eekh HOH-fuh!","en":"I hope so!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I will travel soon","answer":"Ich werde bald reisen"},{"type":"fill","q":"Wirst du Deutsch ___? (learn)","answer":"lernen"},{"type":"choose","q":"'He will learn fast' is…","options":["Er lernt schnell","Er wird schnell lernen","Er hat schnell gelernt","Er lernte schnell"],"answer":"Er wird schnell lernen"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: reisen / werde / Spanien / nach / ich","answer":"ich werde nach Spanien reisen"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ich werde nach Spanien reisen.","answer":"Ich werde nach Spanien reisen."}],"quiz":[{"q":"ICH WERDE REISEN means…","options":["I travel","I travelled","I will travel","I want travel"],"answer":2,"why":"Werde + verb = future."},{"q":"The main verb in the future goes…","options":["second","to the end","first","nowhere"],"answer":1,"why":"Ich werde … REISEN."},{"q":"NÄCHSTES JAHR is…","options":["last year","next year","this year","every year"],"answer":1,"why":"Nächstes = next."},{"q":"DU WIRST vs DU WERDE: correct is…","options":["du werde","du wirst","both","neither"],"answer":1,"why":"Du WIRST — irregular!."},{"q":"LERNEN means…","options":["to teach","to learn","to study","to forget"],"answer":1,"why":"Lernen = to learn."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Future worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["to travel","to learn","soon"],"key":["reisen","lernen","bald"]},{"instruction":"Put REISEN in the future.","items":["I will travel","you will travel","he will travel"],"key":["ich werde reisen","du wirst reisen","er wird reisen"]},{"instruction":"Talk next year.","items":["What will you do next year?","I will travel to Spain"],"key":["Was wirst du nächstes Jahr machen?","Ich werde nach Spanien reisen"]}]}},{"id":"B1-U3-L2","title":"Media and pronouns (ihn/sie/es)","learn":"Replace things: ICH SEHE DEN FILM → ICH SEHE IHN (I see it). IHN (him/it-m), SIE (her/it-f/them), ES (it-n). German pronouns stand AFTER the verb — no jumping like French!","vocab":[{"t":"die Nachrichten","r":"dee NAHKH-rikh-ten","en":"news","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Sendung","r":"dee ZEN-doong","en":"TV show","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Film","r":"dehr film","en":"film","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Serie","r":"dee ZEH-ree-uh","en":"series","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Kanal","r":"dehr kah-NAHL","en":"channel","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Werbung","r":"dee VEHR-boong","en":"advert","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Schauspieler","r":"dehr SHOW-shpee-ler","en":"actor","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Bildschirm","r":"dehr BILT-sheerm","en":"screen","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Accusative pronouns: ihn/sie/es","explain":"ICH SEHE IHN (I see him/it-m). ICH SEHE SIE (her/it-f OR them!). ICH SEHE ES (it-n). SIE does triple duty: she, they, and formal You (capital SIE)!","pattern":"verb + ihn/sie/es (after the verb!)","examples":[{"t":"Ich sehe sie jeden Tag.","r":"eekh ZEH-uh zee YEH-den tahk.","en":"I see it (the series) every day."},{"t":"Weißt du es?","r":"veyest doo ess?","en":"Do you know it?"},{"t":"Ich verstehe ihn nicht.","r":"eekh fehr-SHTEH-uh een neekht.","en":"I don't understand him/it."}],"mistakes":["Putting pronouns before the verb (French style) — German keeps them AFTER.","Using IHN for feminine things: DIE Serie → SIE."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Lena","t":"Siehst du die Nachrichten?","r":"zeest doo dee NAHKH-rikh-ten?","en":"Do you watch the news?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Ja, ich sehe sie jeden Abend.","r":"yah, eekh ZEH-uh zee YEH-den AH-bent.","en":"Yes, I watch them every evening."},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Magst du die neue Serie?","r":"mahkst doo dee NOY-uh ZEH-ree-uh?","en":"Do you like the new series?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Ja, ich sehe sie freitags.","r":"yah, eekh ZEH-uh zee FRY-tahks.","en":"Yes, I watch it on Fridays."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I see it (the film)","answer":"Ich sehe ihn"},{"type":"fill","q":"Weißt du ___? (it)","answer":"es"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I watch them (news) every evening' is…","options":["Ich sehe sie jeden Abend","Ich sie sehe jeden Abend","Sie sehe ich jeden Abend","Ich sehe es jeden Abend"],"answer":"Ich sehe sie jeden Abend"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: sie / sehe / freitags / ich","answer":"ich sehe sie freitags"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ich sehe sie jeden Abend.","answer":"Ich sehe sie jeden Abend."}],"quiz":[{"q":"ICH SEHE SIE (Serie) means…","options":["I see her/it","she sees me","we see it","they see us"],"answer":0,"why":"Sehe + sie = I see it (f)."},{"q":"DER FILM is…","options":["show","film","news","advert"],"answer":1,"why":"Film = film."},{"q":"German pronouns go…","options":["before the verb","after the verb","at sentence end","nowhere"],"answer":1,"why":"Ich sehe IHN — after!"},{"q":"DIE NACHRICHTEN are…","options":["films","news","series","adverts"],"answer":1,"why":"Nachrichten = news."},{"q":"ICH VERSTEHE IHN NICHT means…","options":["I know him","I don't understand him/it","I see him","I want it"],"answer":1,"why":"Nicht negates at the end."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Media worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["news","film","screen"],"key":["die Nachrichten","der Film","der Bildschirm"]},{"instruction":"Replace with ihn/sie/es.","items":["Ich sehe den Film → …","Ich sehe die Serie → …","Weißt du die Antwort? → …"],"key":["Ich sehe ihn","Ich sehe sie","Weißt du sie?"]},{"instruction":"TV habits.","items":["Do you watch the news?","Yes, I watch them every evening"],"key":["Siehst du die Nachrichten?","Ja, ich sehe sie jeden Abend"]}]}}]}],"test":{"title":"B1 final test","items":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: It was sunny","answer":"Es war sonnig"},{"type":"fill","q":"Dieses Buch ist ___ (better)","answer":"besser"},{"type":"choose","q":"Formal 'Do you speak English?'","options":["Sprichst du Englisch?","Sprechen Sie Englisch?","Spreche ich Englisch?","Sprechen sie Englisch?"],"answer":"Sprechen Sie Englisch?"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I would like to travel","answer":"Ich möchte reisen"},{"type":"translate_t","q":"Du hast recht.","answer":"You are right."},{"type":"fill","q":"Es ist größer ___ mein Haus (than)","answer":"als"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: sonnig / war / es","answer":"es war sonnig"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ich möchte nach Spanien reisen.","answer":"Ich möchte nach Spanien reisen."},{"type":"fill","q":"Ich sehe ___ jeden Abend. (them - news)","answer":"sie"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I will travel soon'","options":["Ich reise bald","Ich werde bald reisen","Ich habe bald gereist","Ich reiste bald"],"answer":"Ich werde bald reisen"}]}}}